# smutHub — permanent redirects (Cloudflare Workers static assets)
#
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]   — see
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
# Limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules. Query strings on the incoming
# request are preserved and re-appended to the destination automatically,
# so /smuthub-app.html?q=Powerless lands on /search?q=Powerless.
#
# The search page was renamed smuthub-app.html -> search.html (serving at
# /search) before launch. These 301s keep every previously-shared link,
# bookmark, and indexed URL working, and tell crawlers the move is permanent
# so ranking signals transfer to the new URL.
/smuthub-app.html  /search  301
/smuthub-app       /search  301

# The dashboard's canonical file retains .html. Force the clean route there so
# Workers static-asset negotiation cannot resolve an older extensionless asset.
/dashboard  /dashboard.html  301

# The book collection + detail pages moved /book/ -> /books/ before launch
# (plural is the convention for a collection that parents its detail pages).
# The splat preserves the rest of the path AND the query string, so
# /book/powerless-roberts-2023/ -> /books/powerless-roberts-2023/ and
# /book/?tag=trope:fae -> /books/?tag=trope:fae. The bare /book has its own
# rule because a splat needs a trailing segment to match.
/book/*  /books/:splat  301
/book    /books         301

# The spice guide now lives inside the public guides content hub. Keep all
# legacy forms working permanently so bookmarks and search signals transfer.
/spice/   /guides/spice-levels/  301
/spice    /guides/spice-levels/  301
/spice/*  /guides/spice-levels/:splat  301

# Bookcase page renamed to /bookshelf/ (2026-07)
/smuthub-bookcase.html  /bookshelf/  301
/smuthub-bookcase  /bookshelf/  301

# The standalone field kit was consolidated into the Gift Compass.
